INSERT INTO `Ability` VALUES ('HBR','AEF','AEF','CAL','AC','Acrobatic','Each time this operative is activated, it can perform a free Dash action during that activation.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','CAL','FTS','From The Shadows','Each time this operative is attacked, for that attack, worsen the BS and WS characteristics of the ranged and melee weapons of the attacker by 1 respectively.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','CAL','LRF','Lightning Reflexes','This operative has a 4+ Invulnerable Save.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','CAL','NR','*Neural','Each time this operative makes a shooting attack with this weapon,\nin the Roll Attack Dice step of that attack, for each hit retained, \nroll a number of D6 equal to the APL characteristic of the target:\non each 4+, inflict 3 Mortal Wounds.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','CUL','AB','Abomination','This operative can never be targeted or affected by Psychic actions.<br/>\nWhile an operative is within [PENT] of a CULEXUS ASSASSIN operative, it cannot perform psychic actions.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','CUL','FTS','From The Shadows','Each time this operative is attacked, for that attack, worsen the BS and WS characteristics of the ranged and melee weapons of the attacker by 1 respectively.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','CUL','LD','Life Drain','Each time this operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack,\nif it incapacitates the enemy operative in that combat or shooting attack,\nit regains 1D3 lost Wounds.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','CUL','LRF','Lightning Reflexes','This operative has a 4+ Invulnerable Save.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','EVS','BMD','Bio-Meltdown','If this operative is incapacitated, roll 1D6 for each operative within [CIRCLE] of this operative.\nOn a 3+, that operative suffers 2D3 Mortal Wounds.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','EVS','FTS','From The Shadows','Each time this operative is attacked, for that attack, worsen the BS and WS characteristics of the ranged and melee weapons of the attacker by 1 respectively.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','EVS','LRF','Lightning Reflexes','This operative has a 4+ Invulnerable Save.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','EVS','NT','*Neurotoxins','Each time a friendly operative fights in combat with this weapon,\nin the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat, for each Critical Hit retained,\nroll a number of D6 equal to the number of Wounds on the target: on each 5+, inflict 1 Mortal Wound.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','VND','FTS','From The Shadows','Each time this operative is attacked, for that attack, worsen the BS and WS characteristics of the ranged and melee weapons of the attacker by 1 respectively.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','VND','LRF','Lightning Reflexes','This operative has a 4+ Invulnerable Save.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','VND','SM','Spymask','The ranged weapon this operative is equipped with gain the No Cover special rule.'),('HBR','AEF','AEF','VND','SS','Stealth Suit','Each time a shooting attack is made against this operative,\nin the Roll Defence Dice step of that shooting attack,\nbefore rolling your Defence Dice, if it is in Cover,\none additional die can be retained as a successful normal save as a result of cover.'),('IMP','AES','AES','CAST','EF','Engendered Focus','You can ignore any or all modifiers to this operative\'s characteristics (including modifiers to the weapons it is equipped with, but excluding its Defence characteristic).'),('IMP','AES','AES','CAST','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','CAST','ZD','Zealous Dedication','Each time this operative would lose a wound, roll 1D6: on a 6, that wound is not lost.'),('IMP','AES','AES','CHI','MED','Medic!','Once per Turning Point, the first time another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative would be incapacitated while Visible To and within [SQUARE] of this operative and not within Engagement Range of an enemy operative,\nif this operative is not within Engagement Range fo an enemy operative, this operative can revive it.\nThat friendly operative is not incapacitated, has 1 wound remaining, and if it was a shooting attack, any remaining attack dice are discarded.\nThat friendly operative can then perform a free Dash action but must finish that move within [TRI] of this operative.\nSubtract 1 from both operatives\' APL.'),('IMP','AES','AES','CHI','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','GNR','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','LSH','AP','Attack Pattern','When this operative is selected for deployment, select one of the following attack patterns for a friendly R-VR CYBER-MASTIFF operative to have for the battle:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Aggressive:</strong> Melee weapons it is equipped with gain the Relentless special rule</li>\n<li><strong>Swift:</strong> Add [CIRCLE] to its Movement characteristic</li>\n<li><strong>Defensive:</strong> Improve its Save characteristic by 1</li>\n</ul>'),('IMP','AES','AES','LSH','HND','Handler','Each time this operative is activated, you can also activate a ready friendly R-VR CYBER-MASTIFF operative at the same time.\nComplete their actions in any order.'),('IMP','AES','AES','LSH','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','MAL','ACF','Accute Focus','Once per Turning Point, during this operative\'s activation, it can perform a mission action or the Pick Up action for one less Action Point (to a minimum of 0 AP).'),('IMP','AES','AES','MAL','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','MRK','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','PE','AS','Assault Shield','If this operative is equipped with a Dominator Maul & Assault Shield, it has a 3+ Save characteristic.'),('IMP','AES','AES','PE','NUN','Nuncio-Aquila','<ul>\n<li>Each time an enemy operative would perform a mission action or the Pick Up action, if that enemy operative is within [SQUARE] of your Nuncio-Aquila token (or this operative if that token has not been placed),\none additional Action Point must be subtracted to perform that action.\nSee the Deploy Nuncio-Aquila action for how that token is placed.</li>\n<li>When determining control of an objective marker your Nuncio-Aquila token (or this operative if that token has not been placed) is within [SQUARE] of,\ntreat enemy operative\'s total APL as being 1 less. Note that this is not a modifier.</li>\n</ul>'),('IMP','AES','AES','PE','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','PE','REP','*Repress','Each time this operative fights in combat with this weapon, you are the Attacker (i.e. even if this operative is not the active operative). If both operatives have this special rule, it has no effect.'),('IMP','AES','AES','PE','SHD','*Shield','Each time this operative fights in combat with this weapon, in the Resolve Successful Hits step of that combat,\neach time it parries, two of your opponent\'s successful hits are discarded (instead of one).'),('IMP','AES','AES','REV','FITF','First In The Field','At the end of the Initiative Phase of the first Turning Point, if this operative is wholly within your drop zone, it can perform a free Normal Move action as if it can FLY.'),('IMP','AES','AES','REV','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','RVR','BST','Beast','Other than the Gather Evidence mission action, this operative cannot perform mission actions and cannot be equipped with equipment.'),('IMP','AES','AES','SUB','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','SUB','REP','*Repress','Each time this operative fights in combat with this weapon, you are the Attacker (i.e. even if this operative is not the active operative).\nIf both operatives have this special rule, it has no effect.'),('IMP','AES','AES','SUB','SHD','*Shield','Each time this operative fights in combat with this weapon, in the Resolve Successful Hits step of that combat,\neach time it parries, two of your opponent\'s successful hits are discarded (instead of one).'),('IMP','AES','AES','VIG','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES','AES','VOX','REFF','Ruthless Efficiency','<i class=\"noprint\">Arbitrators have long experience in claustrophobic confrontations and synchronise their tactics to eliminate foes.\n With chilling precision, they open fire on the guilty even in the press of combat.<br/><br/></i>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that does not have the Blast special rule or the word \"Grenade\" in its name,\n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, enemy operatives within [PENT] of it can have other friendly operatives within Engagement Range and still be selected as a valid target\n (they must still be a valid target by all other means).<br/>\n Each time a friendly operative with this ability makes a shooting attack with a weapon that doesn’t have the Blast special rule or the word ‘grenade’ in its name, \n if the target is within [CIRCLE] of another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative, that ranged weapon has the P1 critical hit rule for that shooting attack.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CAST','CA','Castigator\'s Arrest','Whenever an enemy operative is within control range of this operative, if no other enemy operatives are within this operative’s control range, that enemy operative cannot perform the Fall Back action.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CAST','EF','Engendered Focus','You can ignore any changes to this operative’s stats (including its weapons’ stats, but excluding its Save stat).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CAST','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CAST','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CAST','ZD','Zealous Dedication','Whenever an attack dice inflicts damage of 3 or more on this operative, roll one D6: on a 5+, subtract 1 from that inflicted damage.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CHI','MDC','Medic!','The first time during each turning point that another friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative would be removed from the killzone as incapacitated while visible to and within 3\" of this operative,\nyou can use this rule, providing neither this nor that operative is within control range of an enemy operative.\nIf you do, that friendly operative isn’t incapacitated and has 1 wound remaining. That friendly operative can then immediately perform a free Dash action, but must end that move within this operative’s\ncontrol range. Subtract 1 from this and that operative’s APL stats until the end of their next activations respectively, and if this rule was used during that\nfriendly operative’s activation, that activation ends. You cannot use this rule if this operative is incapacitated.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CHI','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','CHI','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','GNR','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','GNR','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','LSH','AP','Attack Pattern','STRATEGIC GAMBIT in the first turning point. Select one of the following attack patterns for a friendly EXACTION SQUAD R-VR CYBER-MASTIFF operative to have for the battle:\n<ul>\n<li>Aggressive: Its melee weapons have the Relentless weapon rule.</li>\n<li>Swift: Add 2\" to its Move stat.</li>\n<li>Defensive: Improve its Save stat by 1.</li>\n</ul>'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','LSH','HND','Handler','Whenever this operative is activated, you can activate a ready friendly EXACTION SQUAD R-VR CYBER-MASTIFF operative at the same time. Complete their activations action by action in any order.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','LSH','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','LSH','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','MAL','AF','Acute Focus','Once during each of this operative’s activations, it can perform the Pick Up Marker, Place Marker, Veriscant or a mission action for 1 less AP.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','MAL','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','MAL','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','MRK','CP','*Concealed Position','This operative can only use this weapon the first time it’s performing the Shoot action during the battle.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','MRK','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','MRK','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','PE','AS','Assault Shield','If this operative has a dominator maul & assault shield, it has a 3+ Save stat.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','PE','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','PE','NA','Nuncio-Aquila','<ul>\n<li>Whenever an enemy operative is within 3\" of your Nuncio-aquila marker (or this operative if your Nuncio-aquila marker isn’t in the killzone), your opponent must spend 1 additional AP for that enemy operative to perform the Pick Up Marker and mission actions.</li>\n<li>Whenever determining control of a marker, treat the total APL stat of enemy operatives that contest it as 1 lower if at least one of those enemy operatives is within 3\" of your Nuncio-aquila marker\n(or this operative if your Nuncio-aquila marker isn’t in the killzone). Note this isn’t a change to the APL stat, so any changes are cumulative with this</li>\n</ul>'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','PE','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','PE','REP','*Repress','Whenever this operative is using this weapon:\n<ul>\n<li>Each of your blocks can be allocated to block two unresolved successes (instead of one).</li>\n<li>If this operative is retaliating, you resolve the first attack dice (i.e. defender instead of attacker).</li>\n</ul>'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','REV','FITF','First In The Field','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> in the first turning point.\nIf this operative is wholly within your drop zone, it can immediately perform a free Reposition action.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','REV','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','REV','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','RVR','BST','Beast','This operative cannot perform any actions other than Apprehend, Charge, Dash, Fall Back, Fight, Guard, Reposition, Pick Up Marker and Place Marker. It cannot use any weapons that aren’t on its datacard.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','RVR','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','RVR','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','SUB','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','SUB','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','SUB','REP','*Repress','Whenever this operative is using this weapon:\n<ul>\n<li>Each of your blocks can be allocated to block two unresolved successes (instead of one).</li>\n<li>If this operative is retaliating, you resolve the first attack dice (i.e. defender instead of attacker).</li>\n</ul>'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','SUB','SS','Stubborn Subjugator','You can ignore any changes to the Hit stat of this operative’s melee weapons.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','VIG','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','VIG','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','VIG','SQV','Close Quarters Vigilance','This operative can perform the Shoot action (excluding Guard) while within control range of an enemy operative, but only if it hasn’t performed the Charge action during the activation,\nor if it’s a counteraction. Note this operative isn’t restricted from performing the Charge action after performing the Shoot action.'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','VOX','MFJ','Marked For Justice','<strong>STRATEGIC GAMBIT</strong> Select one enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point.\nWhenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against your mark, that friendly operative’s weapons have the Punishing weapon rule.\nWhenever your mark is incapacitated, you can select a new enemy operative to be your mark for the turning point (and can continue to do so during this turning point).'),('IMP','AES24','AES24','VOX','RE','Ruthless Efficiency','Whenever a friendly EXACTION SQUAD operative is shooting (excluding with frag or krak grenades) and you’re selecting a valid target, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, having other friendly EXACTION SQUAD operatives within an enemy operative’s control range doesn’t prevent that enemy operative from being selected.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','ASGT','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','ASGT','CVET','Chapter Veteran','At the end of the Select Operatives step, if this operative is selected for deployment, select one additional CHAPTER TACTIC for it to have for the battle.\nUnlike primary and secondary CHAPTER TACTICS, you don\'t have to select the same one for each battle in a campaign or tournament.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','ASGT','DW','Doctrine Warfare','Whenever you would use the Combat Doctrine strategic ploy and then select Assault or Tactical, if this operative is in the killzone, it costs you 0CP.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','AWAR','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','CPT','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','CPT','HL','Heroic Leader','Once per turning point, you can use a firefight ploy for 0CP if this is the specified ANGEL OF DEATH operative (excluding Command Re-roll),\nor the Adjust Doctrine firefight ploy for 0CP if this operative is in the killzone and not within control range of enemy operatives.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','CPT','IH','Iron Halo','Once per battle, when an attack die inflicts Normal Damage on this operative, you can ignore that inflicted damage.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','GNR','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','GRN','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','GRN','GRN','Grenadier','This operative can use frag and krak grenades (see universal equipment).\nDoing so does not count towards any limited uses you have (i.e. if you also select those grenades from equipment for other operatives).\nWhenever it is doing so, improve the Hit stat of that weapon by 1.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','HGNR','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','ISGT','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','ISGT','CVET','Chapter Veteran','At the end of the Select Operatives step, if this operative is selected for deployment, select one additional CHAPTER TACTIC for it to have for the battle.\nUnlike primary and secondary CHAPTER TACTICS, you don\'t have to select the same one for each battle in a campaign or tournament.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','ISGT','DW','Doctrine Warfare','Whenever you would use the Combat Doctrine strategic ploy and then select Devastator or Tactical, if this operative is in the killzone, it costs you 0CP.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','SNP','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','SNP','CC','Camo Cloak','Whenever an operative is shooting this operative, ignore the Saturate weapon rule.\nThis operative has the Stealthy CHAPTER TACTIC. If you selected that CHAPTER TACTIC, you can do both of its options (i.e. retain two cover saves – one normal and one critical success).'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','SNP','ST','Stealthy','Whenever an operative is shooting this operative, if you can retain any cover saves, you can retain one additional cover save, or you can retain one cover save as a critical success.\nThis is not cumulative with improved cover saves from Vantage terrain.'),('IMP','AOD','AOD','WAR','AS','Astartes','During each friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative\'s activation, it can perform either two Shoot actions or two Fight actions.\nIf it\'s two Shoot actions, a bolt weapon must be selected for at least one of them, and if it\'s a bolt sniper rifle or heavy bolter, 1 additional AP must be spent for the second action if both actions are using that weapon.<br/>\nEach friendly ANGEL OF DEATH operative can counteract regardless of its order.'),('SPEC','ATP','ATP','PRI','ELP','Extremis-Level Psyker','<ul>\n<li>This operative can perform two Shoot actions during its activation, but it cannmot use each of its Ranged Weapons more than once per Turning Point</li>\n<li>This operative is such a powerful Psyker that enemy operatives\' abilities that affect this operative when it performs psychic actions (or prevent it from doin so) have no effect.</li>\n</ul>'),('SPEC','ATP','ATP','PRI','WFC','Warp-Fueled Constitution','<ul>\n<li>This operative has a 4+ Invulnerable Save</li>\n<li>Each time this operative would lose a Wound, roll 1D6: on a 5+, that Wound is not lost</li>\n</ul>'),('SPEC','ATP','ATP','THR','MW','Mastered Will','Each time a friendly PRISONER operative Visible to and within [CIRCLE] of this operative is selected as the target of a combat or shooting attack, you can resolve that combat or shooting attack against this operative instead.'),('SPEC','ATP','ATP','THR','SW','Scavenged Weapons','This operative is equipped with a Firearm and Gun Butt, or a Pistol and Crude Melee Weapon.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','AGIT','DEV','Devoted','Once per Turning Point, when this operative fights in combat, in the Resolve Successful Hits step of that combat, you can ignore the damage inflicted on it from one normal hit.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','AGIT','PC','Psiren Caster','Each time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack against an enemy operative within [PENT] of this operative, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend one Crossfire token for free, even if that enemy operative has none.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','AGIT','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','CMDR','CRD','Coordinate','Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can use this ability instead. If you do so, select one operative Visible To this operative to get a Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','CMDR','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','GNR','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','ICNW','BMD','Broodmind Devotion','Once per Turning Point, when a ready friendly BROOD BROTHER operative would be incapacitated within [PENT] of this operative, you can use this ability. If you do so, before that operative is incapacitated, it can perform one free action (excluding Fight and Mind Control), and you can change its order to do so. It is then incapacitated as normal. You cannot use this ability and the Medic! ability on the same operative at the same time.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','ICNW','CI','Cult Icon','When determining control of an objective marker within [PENT] of this operative, treat the total APL of friendly BROOD BROTHER operatives within the required distance of that objective marker as being 1 higher. Note that this is not a modifier. In Narrative Play, this is cumulative with the Focused Battle Honour.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','ICNW','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','KF','ASS','Assassin','This operative can perform the Charge action while it has a Conceal order.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','KF','CA','Counterattack','Each time this operative fights in combat, in the Resolve Successful Hits step of that combat, each time your opponent resolves a successful normal hit, the enemy operative suffers 1 Mortal Wound.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','KF','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','MAG','SL','Spiritual Leader','Friendly BROOD BROTHER operatives have a 5+ Invulnerable Save, cannot be injured, and their APL cannot be negatively modified.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','MAG','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','MDC','MDC','Medic!','Once per Turning Point, the first time another friendly BROOD BROTHER operative (excluding PATRIARCH) would be incapacitated while Visible To and within [SQUARE] of this operative and not within Engagement Range of an enemy operative,\nif this operative is not within Engagement Range of an enemy operative, this operative can revive it.\nThat friendly operative is not incapacitated, has 1 wound remaining, and if it was a shooting attack, any remaining attack dice are discarded.\nThat friendly operative can then perform a free Dash action but must finish that move within [TRI] of this operative.\nSubtract 1 from both operatives\' APL.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','MDC','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PAT','AP','Alpha Predator','This operative has a 4+ Invulnerable Save. Its APL cannot be modified. You can activate it twice during the Turning Point so long as it has action points to spend (it stays ready while it has), but it cannot move more than [PENT] + [SQUARE] per Turning Point.\nEach time you activate it, generate as many action points for that activation as you wish from its APL (you cannot generate more over the Turnning Point than its APL).'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PAT','MST','Monster','This operative cannot be equipped with Equipment. Light terrain and operatives with a Wounds characteristic of 15 or less do not provide Cover for this operative.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PAT','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PF','ELS','Elusive','This operative can perform mission actions while within Engagement Range of an enemy operative (this takes precedence over cannot). It can move through operatives (it cannot finish a move on their bases), can move within Engagement Range of enemy operatives (it must still finish the move following all requirements for that move), and can finish the Charge action within Engagement Range of any enemy operative.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PF','SMOL','Small','This operative cannot be equipped with equipment. While this operative has a Conceal order, it is always treated as having a Conceal order, regardless of any other rules (e.g. Vantage Point). This operative can perform the Fall Back action for one less action point (to a minimum of 1 AP).'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PF','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PRIM','FOTP','Fist Of The Patriarch','This operative can perform two Fight or Shoot actions during its activation.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PRIM','MM','Mastermind','Once per Turning Point, after rolling off to determine initiative, you can do one of the following:\n<ul>\n<li>Add 1 to your roll</li>\n<li>If you did not have initiative in the previous Turning Point, re-roll your dice</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','PRIM','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','SAP','FD','Final Defiance','If this operative\'s Wounds are reduced to zero or less, it can perform a free Explosives action before it is incapacitated.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','SAP','GND','Grenades','This operative is equipped with Frag and Krak grenades and they do not cost any equipment points for this operative.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','SAP','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','SNP','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','TAC','INT','Interference','Select one enemy operative within [PENT] of a killzone edge (excluding your opponent\'s killzone edge) and roll 1D6: if the result is equal to or greater than that enemy operative\'s APL, subtract 1 from its APL.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','TAC','LKT','Lookout','Select one enemy operative. That operative and all enemy operatives within [CIRCLE] of it gain a Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','TAC','REINF','Reinforcement','Set up one new friendly BROOD BROTHER TROOPER operative with an order of your choice wholly within [PENT] of your killzone edge and not within Engagement Range of an enemy operative. Activate it, and it is treated as having performed the Normal Move action (subtract Action Points accordingly) then continue its activation as normal. You cannot use this Tactical Asset more than once per battle.\n<br/>\nThat friendly TROOPER operative does not need to be on your roster and cannot have any equipment. For Narrative Play, it counts as being selected for deployment (e.g. for Recover Tests), and it does not need to be on your dataslate (if it is not, it is removed from your kill team at the end of the battle).'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','TRP','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','VET','BDG','Bodyguard','You can use the Unquestioning Loyalty Tactical Ploy for 0 CP if this operative is the friendly BROODGUARD operative.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','VET','RES','Resilient','Each time this operative would lose a wound, roll 1D6: on a 5+, that wound is not lost.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','VET','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO','BBRO','VOX','XF','Crossfire','Each time after a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat as the active operative or makes a shooting attack, if the enemy operative is not incapacitated, that enemy operative gains one of your Crossfire tokens.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can spend any number of Crossfire tokens the enemy operative has. For each Crossfire token you spend, you can re-roll one of your Attack Dice, then remove the spent Crossfire token.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','AGIT','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','AGIT','DEV','Devoted','Once per turning point, when this operative is fighting or retaliating, in the Resolve Attack Dice step, you can ignore the damage inflicted on it from one normal success.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','AGIT','PC','Psiren Caster','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative within 6\" of this operative, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','CMDR','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','CMDR','COORD','Coordinate','STRATEGIC GAMBIT. Select one enemy operative to gain one of your Crossfire tokens.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','FAM','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','FAM','ELU','Elusive','This operative can perform mission actions while within control range of an enemy operative (taking precedence over those actions\' normal conditions).\nIt can move through enemy operatives, move within control range of them, and during the Charge action can leave their control range (it must still end the move following all requirements for that move).'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','FAM','GA','Group Activation','Whenever this operative is expended, you must then activate any other ready friendly BROOD BROTHER PSYCHIC FAMILIAR operative (if able) before your opponent activates.\nWhen that other operative is expended, your opponent then activates as normal.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','FAM','smol','Small','This operative cannot use any weapons that are not on its datacard, or perform unique actions.\nWhile this operative has a Conceal order, it is always treated as having a conceal order, taking precedence over all other rules (i.e, vantage terrain).\nThis operative can perform the Fall Back action for 1 less AP.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','GNR','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','IW','BMD','Broodmind Devotion','Once per turning point when a ready friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is incapacitated within 6\" of this operative, you can use this rule.\nIf you do, before that operative is removed from the killzone, it can perform one free action (excluding Fight and Mind Control) and you can change its order to do so.\nIt is then incapacitated as normal.<br/>\nYou cannot use this rule and the Medic! Rule (See MEDIC datacard) on the same operative at the same time.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','IW','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','IW','CI','Cult Icon','Whenever determining control of a marker within 6\" of this operative, treat the total APL stat of friendly BROOD BROTHER operatives that control it as 1 higher if at least one friendly BROOD BROTHER operative contests that marker.\nNote this is not a change to the APL stat, so any changes are cumulative with this.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','KF','ASS','Assassin','This operative can perform the Charge action while it has a Conceal order.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','KF','CA','Counterattack','Whenever this operative is fighting or retaliating, whenever your opponent resolves a normal success, inflict 1 damage on the enemy operative in that sequence.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','KF','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','MAG','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','MAG','SL','Spiritual Leader','Whenever this operative is in the killzone:\n<ul>\n<li>Whenever an enemy operative is shooting a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative, ignore the piercing rule.</li>\n<li>You can ignore any changes to friendly BROOD BROTHER operative\'s stats from being injured (including their weapons\' stats).</li>\n<li>You can ignore any changes to the APL stats of friendly BROOD BROTHER operative.</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','MED','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','MED','MED','Medic!','The first time during each turning point that another friendly BROOD BROTHER operative (excluding PATRIARCH) would be removed from the killzone is incapacitated while visible to and within 3\" of this operative,\nyou can use this rule, providing neither this operative nor that operative is within control range of an enemy operative.\nIf you do, that friendly operative is not incapacitated and has 1 wound remaining.\nThat friendly operative can then immediately perform a free Dash action, but must end that move within this operative\'s control range.\nSubtract 1 from this and that operative\'s APL stats until the end of their next activations respectively, and if this rule was used during that friendly operative\'s activation, that activation ends.<br/>\nYou cannot use this rule if this operative is incapacitated.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','PAT','AP','Alpha Predator','Whenever an operative is shooting this operative, ignore the Piercing weapon rule.\nYou can activate this operative twice during the turning point as long as it has AP to spend (it stays ready while it can still be activated a second time).\nPer turning point it cannot move more than 9\" and you cannot spend more than 4AP in total for it.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','PAT','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','PAT','MNS','Monster','This operative cannot use any weapons that are not on its datacard, or perform unique actions (excluding Into Shadow and Mind Control).\nWhenever your opponent is selecting a valid target, if this operative has a conceal order, it cannot use Light terrain for cover.\nWhile this can allow this operative to be targeted (assuming it is visible), it does not remove its cover save (if any).'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','PRIM','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','PRIM','FOTP','Fist Of The Patriarch','This operative can perform either two shoot or two fight actions during its activation.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','PRIM','MM','Mastermind','Once per turning point, after rolling off to determine initiative, if this operative is in the killzone, you can do one of the following:\n<ul>\n<li>Add 1 to your dice result.</li>\n<li>If you did not have initiative in the previous turning point, re-roll your dice.</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','SAP','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','SAP','FD','Final Defiance','If this operative is incapacitated, it can perform a free Explosives unique action before it is removed from the killzone.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','SAP','GRN','Grenadier','This operative can use frag and krak grenades (see universal equipment).\nDoing so does not count towards any limited uses you have (i.e, if you also select those grenades from equipment for other operatives).\nWhenever it is doing so, improve the Hit stat of that weapon by 1.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','SNP','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','SNP','CP','*Concealed Position','This operative can only use this weapon the first time it is performing the Shoot action during the battle.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','TRP','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','TRP','GA','Group Activation','Whenever this operative is expended, you must then activate any other ready friendly BROOD BROTHER TROOPER operative (if able) before your opponent activates.\nWhen that other operative is expended, your opponent then activates as normal (in other words, you cannot activate more than two operatives as specified with this rule).'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','VET','BG','Bodyguard','You can use the Unquestioning Loyalty firefight ploy for 0 CP if this is the specified friendly BROODGUARD operative.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','VET','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','VET','RES','Resilient','Normal damage of 3 or more inflicts 1 less damage on this operative.'),('TYR','BBRO24','BBRO24','VOX','CF','Crossfire','Whenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against or fighting against an enemy operative, after resolving all of your attack dice, if that enemy operative is not incapacitated it gains one of your Crossfire tokens.<br/>\nWhenever a friendly BROOD BROTHER operative is shooting against, fighting against or retaliating against an enemy operative that has any of your Crossfire tokens, you can remove any of those tokens. For each that you do, you can re-roll one of your attack dice.'),('TYR','BC','AH','IB','IB','Icon Bearer','When determining control of an objective marker, treat this operative\'s APL characteristic as being 1 higher. Note that this is not a modifier. In narrative play, this is cumulative with the Focused Battle Honour (see Kill Team Core Book).'),('TYR','BC','AH','LDR','LW','Lash Whip','While an enemy operative is within Engagement Range of friendly operatives equipped with this weapon, subtract 1 from that enemy operative\'s Attacks characteristic.'),('TYR','BC','HM','IB','IB','Icon Bearer','When determining control of an objective marker, treat this operative\'s APL characteristic as being 1 higher. Note that this is not a modifier. In narrative play, this is cumulative with the Focused Battle Honour (see Kill Team Core Book).'),('TYR','BC','NH','IB','IB','Icon Bearer','When determining control of an objective marker, treat this operative\'s APL characteristic as being 1 higher. Note that this is not a modifier. In narrative play, this is cumulative with the Focused Battle Honour (see Kill Team Core Book).'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','BRG','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','BRG','ED','Explosive Demise','If this operative is incapacitated, you can use this ability. If you do so, roll 1D6, subtracting 1 from the result if this operative is within Engagement Range of an enemy operative:\nOn a 3+, each operative Visible to and within [CIRCLE] of this operative suffers D3 Mortal Wounds.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','BRG','GRND','Grenadier','This operative is equipped with Frag and Krak grenades and they do not cost any equipment points.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','BUT','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','BUT','BO','*Blood Offering','Each time this operative fights in combat with this weapon, in the Resolve Successful Hits step of that combat,\nthe first time you strike with a Critical Hit, add one Blooded token to your pool.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','BUT','US','Unholy Sustenance','Each time this operative fights in combat, if it incapacitates the enemy operative in that combat, it regains D3 lost wounds.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','CHIEF','BI','Blooded Icon','Once per Turning Point, when a friendly BLOODED operative with a Blooded token is incapacitated within [PENT] of this operative, you can add that token to your pool.\nThis has no effect if the operative is only treated as having a Blooded token.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','CHIEF','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','CHIEF','LWS','Lead With Strength','Each time this operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, if it has a Blooded token and is more than [PENT] from your drop zone, treat it as if it is under the gaze of the Gods for that combat or shooting attack.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','COMMS','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','CORPSE','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','CORPSE','RD','Regular Dosage','At the end of the Select a KillTeam step of the mission sequence, if this operative is selected for deployment,\nyou can select one friendly BLOODED operative to gain a Stimm effect.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','ENF','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','ENF','GD','Grueling Disciplinarian','While a friendly BLOODED operative is Visible to and within [SQUARE] of this operative, it is not treated as being injured\n(only ignore the modifier to its Movement characteristic as a result of being injured if it is activated within [SQUARE] of this operative).'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','FLN','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','FLN','ST','*Stalk','Each time this operative fights in combat wit this weapon, if it is within [CIRCLE] of Light or Heavy terrain, this weapon gains the Lethal 5+ special rule for that combat.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','FLN','W','Wretched','This operative can perform a Charge action while it has a Conceal order. If this operative is incapacitated in combat,\nif you have any remaining Attack dice, you can strike with one Attack die before this operative is removed from the killzone.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','GNR','BLD','Blooded','<i class=\"noprint\">Having cast aside their oaths of loyalty to the Golden Throne, these Traitor Guardsmen now seek to catch the eye of a Dark God.\n To this end, they make the battlefield into their sacrificial altar, risking acts of insane bravado to spill enemy blood, and perhaps earn fleeting rewards fo unholy power.\n <br/><br/></i>\n \n Keep a pool of Blooded tokens. Add a Blooded token to your pool as follows:\n <ul>\n <li>At the start of each initiative phase</li>\n <li>The first time an enemy operative is incapacitated in each Turning Point</li>\n <li>The first time a friendly operative is incapacitated within [PENT] of an enemy operative in each Turning Point</li>\n </ul>\n Once in each Strategy Phase, when it is your turn to use a Strategic Ploy or pass, you can assign any or all of your Blooded tokens from your pool to friendly BLOODED operatives in the killzone.\n Each operative can have no more than one Blooded token.<br/>\n In each Strategy Phase, after assigning your Blooded tokens (if any), if four or more friendly operatives in the killzone have Blooded tokens, you can select one of them to be under the gaze of the Gods until the end of the Turning Point.\n <br/>\n Each time a friendly BLOODED operative that has a Blooded token fights in combat or makes a shooting attack, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack,\n before rolling your Attack Dice, you can retain one as a successful normal hit without rolling it.\n If that friendly BLOODED operative is under the gaze of the Gods, you can retain one as a successful critical hit instead.'),('CHAOS','BLD','BLD','OGR