save. Each time this operative is activated, it can perform a free Dash action during that activation.'),('TYR','HF','GS','LDR','SYN','Synapse','<ul>\n	<li>Each time this operative is activated, if it is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, for that activation, do not subtract [CIRCLE] from its Movement characteristic as a result of being injured</li>\n    <li>While this operative is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, do not worsen the Ballistic Skill and Weapon Skill of ranged and melee weapons it is equipped with as a result of being injured</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','HF','TS','HRM','SYN','Synapse','<ul>\n	<li>Each time this operative is activated, if it is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, for that activation, do not subtract [CIRCLE] from its Movement characteristic as a result of being injured</li>\n    <li>While this operative is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, do not worsen the Ballistic Skill and Weapon Skill of ranged and melee weapons it is equipped with as a result of being injured</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','HF','TS','TRM','SYN','Synapse','<ul>\n	<li>Each time this operative is activated, if it is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, for that activation, do not subtract [CIRCLE] from its Movement characteristic as a result of being injured</li>\n    <li>While this operative is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, do not worsen the Ballistic Skill and Weapon Skill of ranged and melee weapons it is equipped with as a result of being injured</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','HF','TW','FTR','SYN','Synapse','<ul>\n	<li>Each time this operative is activated, if it is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, for that activation, do not subtract [CIRCLE] from its Movement characteristic as a result of being injured</li>\n    <li>While this operative is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, do not worsen the Ballistic Skill and Weapon Skill of ranged and melee weapons it is equipped with as a result of being injured</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','HF','TW','FTR','WB','Weaponbeast','If this operative is equipped with two melee weapons, add 1 to their Attacks characteristics.'),('TYR','HF','TW','HGNR','SYN','Synapse','<ul>\n	<li>Each time this operative is activated, if it is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, for that activation, do not subtract [CIRCLE] from its Movement characteristic as a result of being injured</li>\n    <li>While this operative is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, do not worsen the Ballistic Skill and Weapon Skill of ranged and melee weapons it is equipped with as a result of being injured</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','HF','TW','LDR','SYN','Synapse','<ul>\n	<li>Each time this operative is activated, if it is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, for that activation, do not subtract [CIRCLE] from its Movement characteristic as a result of being injured</li>\n    <li>While this operative is injured and within [PENT] of a friendly HIVE FLEET SYNAPSE operative, do not worsen the Ballistic Skill and Weapon Skill of ranged and melee weapons it is equipped with as a result of being injured</li>\n</ul>'),('TYR','HF','TW','LDR','WB','Weaponbeast','If this operative is equipped with two melee weapons, add 1 to their Attacks characteristics.'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','APP','LM','Living Metal','<em class=\"noprint\">The Necrons\' semi-sentient metal skin lets them heal mid-battle.\nGlowing grooves cut in the living armour are mended as the skin reforms, and enemy shots that have driven deep into the Necrons\' skin are pushed out, leaving not a scratch.<br/><br/></em>\n\nIn the Ready Operatives step of each Initiative phase, this operative regains up to 2 lost Wounds\n(or up to 1 lost Wound if it is a PLASMACYTE operative).'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','APP','MAGC','Magnification Conduit','Each time this operative makes a shooting attack, if a friendly CRYPTEK operative has an Engage order and is Visible To this operative, \n in the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, you can treat that friendly CRYPTEK operative as the active operative for the purposes of determining Line Of Sight.\n If you do so, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that shooting attack, you can re-roll any or all of your attack dice results of one result (e.g. results of 2).'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','APP','RAP','Reanimation Protocols','<em class=\"noprint\">Should a Necron be slain, its body becomes wreathed in an eerie glow. Crawling limbs reattach, sundered torsos and smashed skulls mend amidst emerald sparks, and the Necron rises again.\nThose too catastrophically damaged to reform vanish instead, teleported away to their tombs for repair.<br/><br/></em>\n\nCertain rules allow friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operatives to attempt reanimation (e.g. Reanimation Beam).\nThe first time each friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operative is incapacitated, if it attempts reanimation, before removing that operative from the killzone,\nplace one of your Reanimation tokens underneath the operative as close as possible to the centre of its base and leave its order token next to it.\nNote that the second time each friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operative is incapacitated, it cannot attempt reanimation.\n\nIn the Ready Operatives step of each Turning Point, roll 1D6 for each of your Reanimation tokens.\nOn 1, leave that Reanimation token in the kill zone. On a 2+, an operative is successfully reanimated:\n<ul>\n<li>Set up the operative that Reanimation token was placed for.</li>\n<li>It must be placed within [SQUARE] of that Reanimation token and not within Engagement Range of enemy operatives.</li>\n<li>It has 1D3 + 2Wounds remaining.</li>\n<li>It has an order of your choice.</li>\n<li>Remove that Reanimation token.\n</ul>\n<br/>\nIn Narrative Play, operatives that are successfully reanimated are not treated as being incapacitated for the purposes of Casualty tests unless they are incapacitated again during that battle.'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','CHRON','LM','Living Metal','<em class=\"noprint\">The Necrons\' semi-sentient metal skin lets them heal mid-battle.\nGlowing grooves cut in the living armour are mended as the skin reforms, and enemy shots that have driven deep into the Necrons\' skin are pushed out, leaving not a scratch.<br/><br/></em>\n\nIn the Ready Operatives step of each Initiative phase, this operative regains up to 2 lost Wounds\n(or up to 1 lost Wound if it is a PLASMACYTE operative).'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','CHRON','MAGC','Magnification Conduit','Each time this operative makes a shooting attack, if a friendly APPRENTEK operative has an Engage Order and is Visible To this operative, \nin the Select Valid Target step of that shooting attack, you can treat that friendly APPRENTEK operative as the active operative for the purposes of determining Line Of Sight.\nIf you do so, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that shooting attack, you can re-roll any or all of your attack dice results of one result (e.g. results of 2).'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','CHRON','RAP','Reanimation Protocols','<em class=\"noprint\">Should a Necron be slain, its body becomes wreathed in an eerie glow. Crawling limbs reattach, sundered torsos and smashed skulls mend amidst emerald sparks, and the Necron rises again.\nThose too catastrophically damaged to reform vanish instead, teleported away to their tombs for repair.<br/><br/></em>\n\nCertain rules allow friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operatives to attempt reanimation (e.g. Reanimation Beam).\nThe first time each friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operative is incapacitated, if it attempts reanimation, before removing that operative from the killzone,\nplace one of your Reanimation tokens underneath the operative as close as possible to the centre of its base and leave its order token next to it.\nNote that the second time each friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operative is incapacitated, it cannot attempt reanimation.\n\nIn the Ready Operatives step of each Turning Point, roll 1D6 for each of your Reanimation tokens.\nOn 1, leave that Reanimation token in the kill zone. On a 2+, an operative is successfully reanimated:\n<ul>\n<li>Set up the operative that Reanimation token was placed for.</li>\n<li>It must be placed within [SQUARE] of that Reanimation token and not within Engagement Range of enemy operatives.</li>\n<li>It has 1D3 + 2Wounds remaining.</li>\n<li>It has an order of your choice.</li>\n<li>Remove that Reanimation token.\n</ul>\n<br/>\nIn Narrative Play, operatives that are successfully reanimated are not treated as being incapacitated for the purposes of Casualty tests unless they are incapacitated again during that battle.'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','DM','LM','Living Metal','<em class=\"noprint\">The Necrons\' semi-sentient metal skin lets them heal mid-battle.\nGlowing grooves cut in the living armour are mended as the skin reforms, and enemy shots that have driven deep into the Necrons\' skin are pushed out, leaving not a scratch.<br/><br/></em>\n\nIn the Ready Operatives step of each Initiative phase, this operative regains up to 2 lost Wounds\n(or up to 1 lost Wound if it is a PLASMACYTE operative).'),('NEC','HIER','HIER','DM','RAP','Reanimation Protocols','<em class=\"noprint\">Should a Necron be slain, its body becomes wreathed in an eerie glow. Crawling limbs reattach, sundered torsos and smashed skulls mend amidst emerald sparks, and the Necron rises again.\nThose too catastrophically damaged to reform vanish instead, teleported away to their tombs for repair.<br/><br/></em>\n\nCertain rules allow friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operatives to attempt reanimation (e.g. Reanimation Beam).\nThe first time each friendly HIEROTEK CIRCLE operative is incapacitated, if it attempts reanimation, before removing that operative from th