 in the kill zone.\n<ul>\n<li>While an enemy operative is within [SQUARE] of your Attack token, each time a friendly HEARTHKYN SALVAGER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack against it, in the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, you can re-roll one of your Attack dice.</li>\n<li>While a friendly HEARTHKYN SALVAGER operative is within [SQUARE] of your Defend Token, each time a shooting attack is made against it, in the Roll Defence Dice step of that shooting attack, you can re-roll one of your Defence dice.</li>\n<li>At the end of each Turning Point, remove your Attack token or Defend token.</li>\n</ul>'),('VOT','HKS','HKS','LOK','ED','Early Detection','In the Set Up Operatives step, enemy operatives that are set up in the kill zone cannot be outside of their drop zone (unless mission specifies). In addition, enemy operatives cannot move before the battle begins (although your opponent can still select the Recon scouting option for the purpose of determining initiative).'),('VOT','HKS','HKS','LOK','GR','Grudge','<em class=\"noprint\">If a particular foe shames or insults the Kin gravely enough, they will become the subject of a Grudge.\nTo destry this most hated enemy, the Kin will go to any lengths, even if it is to their own detriment.<br/></em>\nEach time an enemy operative incapacitates a friendly HEARTHKYN SALVAGER operative, that enemy operative gains a Grudge token.\n<br/>\nEach time a friendly HEARTHKYN SALVAGER operative fights in combat or makes a shooting attack against an enemy operative,\nin the Roll Attack Dice step of that combat or shooting attack, for each Grudge token that enemy operative has, you can retain one of your successful Normal hits as a Critical hit instead.'),('VOT','HKS','HKS','LOK','SA','Steady Advance','<em class=\"noprint\">The Kin are a robust and pragmatic people, used to hard lives in the galactic core where danger is to be foun aplenty on uncharted worlds and asteroids. Thus they are well trai